// Without the bottom bar the navigation bar is cleared here:
// KomiBottomBar covers it when the bar is present, and
// KomiScaffold no longer reserves it.

comments.existing_code:
// Screens without the bottom bar must clear the navigation
// bar themselves: the bar covers it when present, and
// KomiScaffold no longer reserves it.

comments.suggestion_code:
modifier =
    if (showBottomBar) {
        Modifier.padding(bottom = bottomBarHeight)
    } else {
        Modifier
            .background(LocalPersonality.current.colors.background)
            .navigationBarsPadding()
    },

// The host reserves the bottom system inset outside this Scaffold (AppNavigation
// pads by the app bottom bar's height when it is shown, or navigationBarsPadding()
// otherwise). Leaving the default insets here made Scaffold reserve the navigation
// bar a second time on devices that report a non-zero bottom inset, cutting every
// page off behind a band the colour of the background. Consumers used outside that
// host must handle the bottom inset themselves.

comments.existing_code:
// The bottom bar lives outside this Scaffold, in AppNavigation, which already
// reserves its height. Leaving the default insets here made Scaffold reserve
// the navigation bar a second time on devices that report a non-zero bottom
// inset, cutting every page off behind a band the colour of the background.

comments.suggestion_code:
contentWindowInsets =
    ScaffoldDefaults.contentWindowInsets
        .only(WindowInsetsSides.Top + WindowInsetsSides.Horizontal)
        // navigationBars is reserved by the app shell (AppNavigation's
        // navigationBarsPadding / the bottom bar), so keep it out entirely.
        .exclude(WindowInsets.navigationBars),
